[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186105745,
      "id": "97cd9132-458b-5234-a3d2-22b633acb74c",
      "title": "Reducing an Augmented Matrix for a Singular 2x2 System to REF and Solving the Resulting System"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-4\\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=-4.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-2y-4,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2y-4\\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix} -2y-4 \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=\u27e8-2y-4,y\u27e9,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/id": "567d0a45-5ee0-5051-b802-8eef876ac84c",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "b192aa1a-2669-58c8-bf49-8d611aa959f8",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
