    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-12\\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=-12.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-2y-12,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2y-12\\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix} -2y-12 \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=\u27e8-2y-12,y\u27e9,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/id": "ec9c499c-06bd-514a-8e1b-72b248c456da",
