  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186105745,
      "id": "97cd9132-458b-5234-a3d2-22b633acb74c",
      "title": "Reducing an Augmented Matrix for a Singular 2x2 System to REF and Solving the Resulting System"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=6\\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-3y=6.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=3y+6,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3y+6\\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix} 3y+6 \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=\u27e83y+6,y\u27e9,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/id": "cb19622d-de26-59ab-8728-6caa8b083d6c",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "0359653a-752e-5317-884b-d36d2cd99a0b",
