    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=2\\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=2-2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2-2y\\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix} 2-2y \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=\u27e82-2y,y\u27e9,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/id": "1fe9d23a-e5fe-57b2-ad1a-05adb7eac86f",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
